        "output.mime_type": "application/json",
        "llm.input_messages.0.message.role": "system",
        "llm.input_messages.0.message.content": "You are a research assistant. Given the research summary and evaluation scores\nbelow, write a clear, concise final answer for the user. Cite sources inline\nusing [1], [2], \u2026 notation matching the sources list.",
        "llm.input_messages.1.message.role": "user",
        "llm.input_messages.1.message.content": "User query: What is the OpenInference semantic convention and how does it extend OpenTelemetry for LLM applications?\n\nResearch summary: The OpenInference semantic convention is a framework designed to extend OpenTelemetry specifically for applications involving large language models (LLMs). It provides a set of conventions that enhance the tracing and monitoring capabilities of OpenTelemetry by addressing the unique requirements of LLM applications. This includes capturing detailed semantic information about the operations and interactions within these models, which is crucial for understanding and optimizing their performance. OpenInference aims to fill the gaps left by traditional telemetry systems when applied to the complex and dynamic nature of LLMs, offering more granular insights into their behavior and performance metrics.\n\nSources:\n[1] https://docs.rs/openinference-semantic-conventions \u2014 openinference_semantic_conventions - Rust... openinference-semantic-conventions 0.1.1... Dependencies opentelemetry ^0.31 normal... About docs.rs...\n[2] https://www.arthur.ai/column/openinference-vs-opentelemetry-genai-conventions-agent-tracing \u2014 OpenInference vs. OpenTelemetry GenAI Conventions: Which Should You Use for Agent Tracing?... OpenInference aims to fill the gaps left by traditional telemetry systems when applied to the complex and dynamic nature of LLMs...\n\nFaithfulness score: 1.00",
        "llm.output_messages.0.message.role": "assistant",
        "llm.output_messages.0.message.content": "The OpenInference semantic convention is a framework that extends OpenTelemetry to better support applications involving large language models (LLMs). It provides specific conventions that enhance the tracing and monitoring capabilities of OpenTelemetry by capturing detailed semantic information about the operations and interactions within LLMs. This is crucial for understanding and optimizing the performance of these models. OpenInference addresses the limitations of traditional telemetry systems when applied to the complex and dynamic nature of LLMs, offering more granular insights into their behavior and performance metrics [1][2].",
